secrets:
  symbol: "#secrets-service"
  description: >
    Seam for secret retrieval (getSecret/requireSecret/getShardedSecret), backing
    #wallet-service, #auth-service, and #worldid-service. getShardedSecret(base,
    shardId) reads `${base}_${shardId}` (e.g. CIRCLE_API_KEY_2) and falls back to the
    plain `base` secret when no shard-specific one is set — used by #wallet-service so
    each wallet shard can eventually get its own scoped Circle credential without
    breaking single-key setups. `SECRETS_BACKEND` (env, default "env") selects the
    backing store: "env" reads plain process.env (unchanged, still not a real AWS/GCP
    Secrets Manager or Vault integration); "ledger-ring" shells out to Ledger's
    `wallet-cli ring decrypt --key <name>` (node:child_process, no device present, only
    network access to restore the trustchain) to retrieve a value that was encrypted at
    rest via a one-time, device-present `wallet-cli ring init` / `ring encrypt` ops
    step — decrypted values are cached in-memory per key per process (same lazy-cache
    pattern as the rest of this file), and any failure (CLI not installed, key missing
    from the ring, non-zero exit, empty output) throws an error naming only the secret
    *name* and a static hint — never the raw stdout/stderr, which could contain partial
    decrypted output or ring diagnostics. See .paradigm/specs/wallet-checkout.md
    "Secrets backend" for the design and the manual device-present provisioning steps
    that can't be scripted, and "Hardening" for the original secrets-manager-ready seam.
